  "query_preview": "..\nTODAY THROUGH FRIDAY PM:\nWeak ridging conditions continue aloft persisting through\nSaturday. A warm front is expected to lift through the CWA by\nFriday morning, advecting above average temperatures with dry\nconditions towards our region. There is a chance of tying/breaking\nFriday's high temperature record (84 degrees - 2004) as \ntemperatures may peak into the upper-80s on Friday. This does pose\na Fire Weather risk potential; high temperatures, low RH values, \nand gusty winds may be conducive for Fire Weather, especially for \nFire Zone 137.\n\nFRIDAY PM THROUGH MONDAY EVENING:\nAfter Friday, anticipate a steep temperature drop off Saturday\nnight into Sunday as a modest cold front sweeps through the region\nwith cooler temperatures to remain, due to consistent CAA.\nSynoptic ascent will be favored with a positively-tilted trough,\noriginating in BC, advancing southward then an eastward motion.\nThis cold front associated with the trough aloft, causing rain and\ntransitioning into a wintry mix. The back side of the low could\nhave a chance of receiving trace amounts of snow. Some areas may\nexperience locally enhanced lift with vorticity with embedded\nperturbations at the mid-levels. It will be dependent upon the \ntemperature profile Sunday night through Monday evening. \n\nTUESDAY ONWARDS:\nDue to an omega blocking pattern to our east, this may stall a\ntrough complex and elevate existing chances of QPF. A mid-level\ntroughing pattern may increase PoPs chances further, should PWAT\nvalues increase with moisture transport. Continued CAA should\nlimit any foreseeable fire weather threats for the time being,\nalbeit after Friday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n -Increased Fire Weather threat Friday.\n\n -Decreased confidence of precipitation type on Sunday through\n  Monday.\n\n -Confidence of forecast track is low.\nFIN",
